 "style": "ballad",
 "text": "Streetlights flicker on the water tonight I keep my hands in my pockets and my eyes on the light You said the city never sleeps but it dreams And every window is a story with a secret in the seams Hold on hold on we're almost home The night is loud but we're not alone Hold on hold on the road is long Sing it back to me I know this song Coffee's cold and the paper's old Every headline is a promise that was never sold You said the summer never ends but it fades And every morning is a window that the sun invades Hold on hold on we're almost home The night is loud but we're not alone Hold on hold on the road is long Sing it back to me I know this song",
